1. First time only: sign up at gitlab.com and verify your account (phone number, sometimes card) -
otherwise pipelines get stuck on "verify your account".
2. On gitlab.com: New project > Create blank project > name GitLabBasicBuild > untick
"Initialize repository with a README" > Create project.
SCREENSHOT 1: Browser - new GitLab project page
3. Download the Q10_GitLabBasicBuild folder from ma'am's Drive (Download all), extract it to the
Desktop and open it in VS Code (File > Open Folder).
4. In Drive, README.md is a Google Doc - open it, copy the text and save it in VS Code as
README.md. Then delete the downloaded .docx copies from the folder.
5. Open .gitlab-ci.yml (from Drive) and replace all its code with:
stages:
- build
build_job:
stage: build
script:
- echo "Starting sample build"
- ls -la
- echo "Build completed successfully"
SCREENSHOT 2: VS Code editor - .gitlab-ci.yml open
SCREENSHOT 3: Browser - GitLab Build > Pipeline editor showing the job
6. Run in terminal (replace YOUR_USERNAME):
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Add GitLab CI build pipeline"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://gitlab.com/YOUR_USERNAME/GitLabBasicBuild.git
git push -u origin main
7. On first push a sign-in window opens - log in to GitLab. If it asks for a password, use an access
token instead: GitLab > Avatar > Preferences > Access tokens > tick write_repository > create
> paste the token as the password.
SCREENSHOT 4: Browser - GitLab project page listing the files
8. GitLab > Build > Pipelines - the pipeline starts by itself; wait for Passed (first run takes 1-3 min;
stuck on "pending" = account not verified).
SCREENSHOT 5: Browser - GitLab Build > Pipelines (status running)
SCREENSHOT 6: Browser - GitLab Build > Pipelines (status Passed)
9. Click the pipeline > build_job to see the job log (Job succeeded).
SCREENSHOT 7: Browser - GitLab build_job log page
